%% HAND-CURATED. Cadence 60s nominal — see sys-03 §6.2.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device
    participant Gateway
    participant DeviceService
    participant PostgreSQL
    participant OfflineSweepWorker

    Device->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/heartbeat {device_id, firmware_version, battery_level, connectivity_metrics} X-Device-Token
    Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
    alt invalid_device_identity
        DeviceService-->>Device: 401 invalid_device_identity (cert revoked or mismatch)
    else device_not_found
        DeviceService-->>Device: 404 (not rate-limited — diagnostic response)
    else device_not_claimed
        DeviceService-->>Device: 403 DEVICE_NOT_CLAIMED (rejected from unclaimed states)
    else heartbeat_rate_limited
        DeviceService-->>Device: 202 heartbeat_ignored (subsequent heartbeat within window, no DB write)
    else success
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE devices SET last_seen_at, firmware_version, battery_level, connectivity_metrics — transition CLAIMED→ACTIVE or OFFLINE→ACTIVE
        DeviceService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT … ON CONFLICT (device_id) DO UPDATE device_heartbeat_snapshots
        PostgreSQL-->>DeviceService: ok
        DeviceService-->>Device: 204 No Content
    end

    Note over OfflineSweepWorker,PostgreSQL: every DEVICE_OFFLINE_SWEEP_INTERVAL_MS (default 60s) — single-owner via advisory lock 0x7B070FF1
    OfflineSweepWorker->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE devices SET status='offline' WHERE state='ACTIVE' AND last_seen_at < now() - DEVICE_OFFLINE_THRESHOLD_SECONDS

    Note over Device,PostgreSQL: timeout 5s p99 · rate-limit AFTER state validation so 404/403 never throttled · onModuleDestroy awaits in-flight sweep
